      "writtenOn": "2025-08-05T20:50:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like it\u0027d be simpler to just do top-down recursion (iteratively, via a worklist) from the `access` instructions that take types containing row-major matrices. That\u0027s the only scenario where you need to chase usages, and from there you can just pass the index that you\u0027re truncating to whatever the load/lve/store/sve is that uses the access, which in turn removes the need for `access_to_vector_index`.\n\nEssentially, I\u0027m suggesting the same structure for processing instructions as the `DecomposeStridedMatrix` transform has. Of course I\u0027m biased towards doing what I did, but I\u0027m really not a fan of these `while(results_to_update.IsEmpty())` loops where you\u0027re adding into that set from various other places.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 121,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 126,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "3d3e2b68462cbca9434f5c4b8d0b707223ccf12c",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "860208c7_141ca36c",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/spirv/reader/lower/transpose_row_major.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 126,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-06T17:59:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I started with the structure of DecomposeStridedMatrix and it didn\u0027t fit well with how this works. The things your changing were sufficiently different that the structure didn\u0027t fit.\n\nThe TransposeRowMajor ends up being more complicated as we have to propagate and update usages of things like LoadVectorElement or split the array access into pieces and access through it. I don\u0027t see that kind of requirement in the DecomposeStridedMatrix?\n\nAs to adding from all over, it actually only adds from the setup loop on 117 and then in the access handling below.",
      "parentUuid": "be6db1e7_03da19d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 121,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 126,
